Here is what was implemented and shipped.

### App: bounded offline kill (`SettingsDrawer.jsx`)

- Added `withTimeout` and **`OFFLINE_KILL_IPC_MS = 12000`** so `llm.cancelStream` and `settings.update` cannot hang the renderer indefinitely.
- On click: **`setStatus({ tone: 'idle', text: 'Applying offline kill switch…' })`** so `data-testid="settings-status-text"` appears immediately (it only renders when `status.text` is set).
- Success still shows **“Offline kill switch engaged…”**; any IPC timeout or error surfaces **“Offline kill switch failed: …”**; **`setBusy(false)`** stays in **`finally`**.

```24:35:c:\Users\KickA\Documents\GitHub\NeuralShell\src\renderer\src\components\SettingsDrawer.jsx
/** Bound IPC waits so connection actions cannot wedge the renderer if main never resolves. */
function withTimeout(promise, ms, label) {
    let timer;
    return Promise.race([
        promise,
        new Promise((_, reject) => {
            timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error(`${label} timed out after ${ms}ms`)), ms);
        }),
    ]).finally(() => clearTimeout(timer));
}

const OFFLINE_KILL_IPC_MS = 12000;
```

